      {% when 'cough-and-cold' %}
<section class="kairali-collection-guide" data-guide="in034-b06-cough-and-cold">
  <h2>Compare these listings by route of use, then by label</h2>
  <p>Some items here are taken by mouth, some are applied on the skin and some are used in the nose. The grid cannot tell you which one suits a particular cough, age or condition.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Start with the person.</strong> Age, pregnancy, allergies, asthma and other conditions change what is appropriate.</li>
    <li><strong>Separate the routes.</strong> Oral, external and nasal items have different directions. Follow only the ones on the pack you choose.</li>
    <li><strong>Read the same facts each time.</strong> Ingredients, age limits, dose, how long it may be used, and any drowsiness, sugar or alcohol note.</li>
  </ul>
  <details><summary>Can I choose something here for a child?</summary><p>Not from the collection. Read the age directions and warnings on the exact label, and ask a qualified professional when the age, symptom or dose is unclear.</p></details>
  <p>Seek prompt care for breathing difficulty, blue or grey lips, chest pain, confusion, dehydration or coughing blood. For wider browsing see <a href="{{ routes.collections_url }}/general-health">general health</a> or <a href="{{ routes.collections_url }}/immunity-and-general-wellness">immunity and general wellness</a>, or book an <a href="/pages/online-consultation">online consultation</a>. Placement here is not a diagnosis.</p>
</section>
      {% when 'abdominal-diseases' %}
<section class="kairali-collection-guide" data-guide="in034-b06-abdominal-diseases">
  <h2>Shop this page by symptom pattern, not by the collection name</h2>
  <p>Pain, bloating, changed bowel habits, nausea and burning have many different causes. This page only groups digestive listings; no single item covers every kind of stomach problem.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Write down the pattern.</strong> Where the discomfort sits, when it began, and whether meals, bowel movements or your medicines change it.</li>
    <li><strong>Check the exact form.</strong> Confirm whether it is an oral powder, tablet, liquid or another form, then follow that label.</li>
    <li><strong>Go narrower where you can.</strong> Compare <a href="{{ routes.collections_url }}/acidity">acidity</a>, <a href="{{ routes.collections_url }}/constipation">constipation</a> and <a href="{{ routes.collections_url }}/gastric-care">gastric care</a> as separate ranges.</li>
  </ul>
  <details><summary>Can I take more than one oral digestive item together?</summary><p>Check each ingredient list and direction for duplication, laxative action and interaction with prescribed medicine, and ask a qualified professional first.</p></details>
  <p>Sudden or severe pain, a rigid abdomen, vomiting blood, black stools, fainting, repeated vomiting, jaundice, or pain or bleeding in pregnancy needs urgent medical attention. Persistent or unexplained symptoms deserve assessment, not another product change.</p>
</section>
      {% when 'hiccough' %}
<section class="kairali-collection-guide" data-guide="in034-b06-hiccough">
  <h2>How long the episode lasts decides your next step</h2>
  <p>Most brief hiccup episodes settle by themselves. Ones that keep returning or will not stop can have varied causes, including illness or a medicine, which this page cannot identify.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Watch the clock.</strong> Note how long an episode lasts, how often it returns, and whether eating, drinking or sleeping is affected.</li>
    <li><strong>Note what is new.</strong> A recent medicine, procedure, illness or added symptom is worth discussing with a qualified professional.</li>
    <li><strong>Read before use.</strong> Compare ingredients, form, directions and warnings on each listing rather than assuming it suits everyone.</li>
  </ul>
  <details><summary>Is a listing here suitable during pregnancy?</summary><p>Not by default. Age, pregnancy, feeding, existing conditions and current medicines all need exact label review and qualified advice.</p></details>
  <p>Breathing difficulty, chest pain, severe abdominal pain, repeated vomiting, or being unable to eat or drink needs assessment, as do hiccups that disturb sleep. <a href="{{ routes.collections_url }}/gastric-care">Gastric care</a> and <a href="{{ routes.collections_url }}/general-health">general health</a> cover wider browsing, and an <a href="/pages/online-consultation">online consultation</a> is available.</p>
</section>
      {% when 'infertility' %}
<section class="kairali-collection-guide" data-guide="in034-b06-infertility">
  <h2>Assessment for both partners comes before any product choice</h2>
  <p>This page groups listings around reproductive wellness. It cannot tell you why conception is taking longer or predict a result. Use it alongside proper care, not instead of it.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Include both partners.</strong> Fertility questions can involve either partner or both, so responsibility should not fall on one person.</li>
    <li><strong>Bring the full picture.</strong> Cycle history, earlier pregnancies, current medicines, health conditions and any tests already done.</li>
    <li><strong>Read the exact label.</strong> Ingredients, directions, warnings and cautions matter most when a care plan is already running.</li>
  </ul>
  <details><summary>Does “herbal” alone establish suitability?</summary><p>No. Ingredients can carry cautions, interactions or pregnancy-related considerations. Discuss planned use with a qualified professional.</p></details>
  <p>Severe pelvic or testicular pain, heavy bleeding, or a positive pregnancy test with pain or bleeding needs urgent attention. <a href="{{ routes.collections_url }}/women-s-health">Women&rsquo;s health</a> and <a href="{{ routes.collections_url }}/men-sexual-health">men&rsquo;s sexual health</a> are separate shopping ranges, and an <a href="/pages/online-consultation">online consultation</a> can guide next steps.</p>
</section>
      {% when 'skin-diseases' %}
<section class="kairali-collection-guide" data-guide="in034-b06-skin-diseases">
  <h2>Describe what changed on the skin before comparing items</h2>
  <p>Rashes, itching, colour change, scaling and sores can look alike without sharing a cause. Listings that look similar may differ in ingredients, route of use and cautions.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Describe the change.</strong> Where it is, how it looks and feels, when it started, and any new product, medicine or exposure.</li>
    <li><strong>Confirm the route first.</strong> Some listings are applied to the skin and others are taken by mouth; read that pack&rsquo;s ingredients, directions, warnings and storage.</li>
    <li><strong>Introduce one change.</strong> When appropriate, avoid several new topical products together.</li>
  </ul>
  <details><summary>Can I choose by the name of a skin condition alone?</summary><p>No. Similar-looking concerns have different causes. Seek qualified assessment when the cause is uncertain, or the problem is persistent, widespread or worsening.</p></details>
  <p>Breathing difficulty, swelling of the lips or eyes, severe pain, fever with a spreading rash or signs of infection needs prompt attention. For routine browsing compare <a href="{{ routes.collections_url }}/skin-care">skin care</a> or the separate <a href="{{ routes.collections_url }}/eczema">eczema range</a>, or request an <a href="/pages/online-consultation">online consultation</a>.</p>
</section>
      {% when 'pruritus' %}
<section class="kairali-collection-guide" data-guide="in034-b06-pruritus">
  <h2>Itching is a symptom; the cause shapes the next step</h2>
  <p>Pruritus means itching. Dryness, irritation, allergy, infection, a medicine or a condition beyond the skin can each present this way, so browsing is not a substitute for assessment.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Look at the pattern.</strong> Where it itches, how long it has lasted, whether there is a rash, and whether anyone else at home is affected.</li>
    <li><strong>Protect the barrier.</strong> Avoid scratching and fragranced experiments, and do not apply anything to broken skin unless that exact label allows it.</li>
    <li><strong>Patch-test where directed.</strong> Read the warnings and stop if irritation or a new reaction appears.</li>
  </ul>
  <details><summary>Can any external item be used on a rash?</summary><p>No. Check the intended use, ingredients, directions and warnings on the exact pack; damaged skin needs that label&rsquo;s permission.</p></details>
  <p>Swelling of the lips or tongue, breathing difficulty, widespread blistering, fever with a rash, or eye or mouth involvement needs prompt medical care. For separate context browse <a href="{{ routes.collections_url }}/skin-diseases">skin concerns</a> or <a href="{{ routes.collections_url }}/skin-care">routine skin care</a>, or request an <a href="/pages/online-consultation">online consultation</a>.</p>
</section>
      {% when 'urine-related-problems' %}
<section class="kairali-collection-guide" data-guide="in034-b06-urine-related-problems">
  <h2>Record the urinary pattern before choosing anything</h2>
  <p>Burning, frequency, urgency, weak flow, pain or a change in the urine can come from an infection, a prostate concern, a stone or a medicine. This page cannot tell those apart.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Note the main change.</strong> When it began, urine colour, where the pain sits, any fever, and difficulty starting or passing urine.</li>
    <li><strong>Compare the exact listing.</strong> Ingredients, oral directions, warnings and interaction advice on the current label.</li>
    <li><strong>Keep prescribed care running.</strong> Do not stop or change prescribed urinary or prostate medicine to try something here; ask the treating clinician.</li>
  </ul>
  <details><summary>Does burning urination always mean an infection?</summary><p>No. Several conditions cause similar symptoms, and testing or examination may be needed to identify the cause.</p></details>
  <p>Being unable to pass urine, fever with flank or back pain, visible blood, or urinary symptoms in pregnancy needs urgent attention. An <a href="/pages/online-consultation">online consultation</a> can guide the next step, <a href="{{ routes.collections_url }}/general-health">general health</a> covers wider browsing, and you can <a href="/pages/contact-us">contact Kairali</a> with product questions.</p>
</section>
